{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyOJea0l+ioo6V8xgXM1dd+j"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Lesson 1: Linear ODEs\n","\n","Finite Difference Approximation\n","- Taylor series:\n","\n","$$f(x)=f(x_j)+(x-x_j)f'(x_j)+\\frac{(x-x_j)^2}{2!}f''(x_j)+\\frac{(x-x_j)^3}{3!}f'''(x_j)+\\mathcal O(x-x_j)^4$$\n","\n","- Truncating at second order and expanding in $\\pm\\Delta x$:\n","\n","$$f(x_{j+1})=f(x_j)+\\Delta xf'(x_j)+\\mathcal O(\\Delta x)^2$$\n","$$f(x_{j-1})=f(x_j)-\\Delta xf'(x_j)+\\mathcal O(\\Delta x)^2$$\n","\n","- 1st Derivative - Forward Difference:\n","$$f'(x_j)=\\frac{f(x_{j+1})-f(x_j)}{\\Delta x}+\\mathcal O(\\Delta x)$$\n","\n","- 1st Derivative - Backward Difference:\n","$$f'(x_j)=\\frac{f(x_{j})-f(x_{j-1})}{\\Delta x}+\\mathcal O(\\Delta x)$$\n","\n","- 1st Derivative - Centered Difference:\n","$$f'(x_j)=\\frac{f(x_{j+1})-f(x_{j-1})}{2\\Delta x}+\\mathcal O(\\Delta x)$$\n","\n","- 2nd Derivative:\n","$$f''(x_j)=\\frac{f(x_{j+1})-2f(x_j)+f(x_{j-1})}{\\Delta x^2}+\\mathcal O(\\Delta x^2)$$\n","Converges as $\\Delta x\\to 0$.\n","\n","- Linear Ordinary Differential Equation\n","\n","$$\\frac{d y(t)}{dt}=-\\lambda y(t) ; t\\in[0,\\infty] ; y(0)=y_0$$\n","\n","where $\\lambda>0$. The exact solution is: $y(t)=y_0e^{-\\lambda t}$\n","\n","Notation:\n","\n","$$n=1,2,.. ; t_n=n\\Delta t ; y^n\\approx y(t_n)$$\n","\n","Truncation error:\n","$$e^n=y(t_n)-y^n$$\n","\n","Approximation (Forward Difference):\n","$$\\frac{y^{n+1}-y^n}{\\Delta t}=-\\lambda y^n$$\n","\n","$$y^{n+1}=(1-\\lambda\\Delta t)y^n$$\n","\n","Converges as $\\Delta t\\to 0$.\n","- Lax Equivalence Theorem:\n","\n","> For a consistent linear method, stability is necessary and sufficient for the convergence.\n","\n","> For nonlinear differental equation, stability of linearized form is necessary, but not sufficient for convergence.\n","\n","> Error $\\epsilon$ can accumulate.\n","\n","- Analysis\n","\n","> $\\Delta t<\\frac{1}{\\lambda}$\n","\n","Stable.\n","\n",">$\\frac{1}{\\lambda}<\\Delta t<\\frac{2}{\\lambda}$\n","\n","Stable but inaccurate.\n","\n",">$\\Delta t>\\frac{2}{\\lambda}$\n","\n","Unstable."],"metadata":{"id":"D_LoC17jJHf-"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Exercise on Linear ODE\n","import numpy as np\n","from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n","\n","#dy/dx\n","def dfxn(x,y):\n","    return -y/2+4*np.exp(-0.5*x)*np.cos(4.0*x)\n","\n","#y(x) exact integral\n","def fxn(x):\n","    return np.exp(-0.5*x)*np.sin(4.0*x)\n","\n","#Euler Forward Scheme\n","def int_eul(x,y,dx):\n","    return y+dx*dfxn(x,y)\n","\n","#Heun's method (Runge-Kutta 2nd Order)\n","def int_heun(x,y,dx):\n","    ystar=y+dx*dfxn(x,y) #Euler part\n","    xp=x+dx\n","    return y+0.5*dx*(dfxn(x,y)+dfxn(xp,ystar))\n","\n","x0=0.0\n","x1=10.0\n","dx=0.1\n","y0=0.0\n","e0=0.0\n","\n","y_eu=y0\n","y_he=y0\n","\n","eul_arr=[0.0,]\n","heun_arr=[0.0,]\n","x_arr=[x0]\n","\n","n=1\n","x=x0\n","\n","while (x < x1):\n","    y_eu=int_eul(x,y_eu,dx) #euler integral\n","    y_he=int_heun(x,y_he,dx) #heun integral\n","    n=n+1\n","    x=x+dx\n","    y_sol=fxn(x) #exact integral\n","    x_arr.append(x) #for graphing purposes\n","    eul_arr.append(y_eu-y_sol) #euler error\n","    heun_arr.append(y_he-y_sol) #heun error\n","\n","plt.plot(x_arr,eul_arr, label='euler')\n","plt.plot(x_arr,heun_arr, label='heun')\n","plt.xlabel('X')\n","plt.ylabel('Error wrt analytical solution')\n","plt.legend( )\n","plt.grid()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":449},"id":"1IZHH7XChNqa","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1771942260255,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":618,"user":{"displayName":"BEATRICE BAYAN","userId":"07825214234165062643"}},"outputId":"2701ecae-e683-474e-9901-c12e199c15f5"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Lesson 2: Linear Advection Equation\n","\n","- Partial Linear Differential Equation:\n","$$\\frac{\\partial\\phi(x,t)}{\\partial t}+u\\frac{\\partial\\phi(x,t)}{\\partial x}=0$$\n","\n","> Where u is constant and $0\\le u\\le1$\n","\n","> Periodic boundary conditions:\n","$\\phi(0,t)=\\phi(1,t)$.\n","\n","> Initial condition:\n","$\\phi(x,0)=F(x)$.\n","\n","> Analytical solution:\n","$$\\phi(x,t)=F(x-ut)$$\n","\n","Linear Advection Equation:\n","> Shape-preserving movement of initial profile $F(x)$ advected with speed $u$ over time $t$.\n","\n","- FTFS: Forward in Time, Forward in Space\n","$$\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_j-\\phi^n_j}{\\Delta t}+u\\frac{\\phi^n_{j+1}-\\phi^n_j}{\\Delta x}=0$$\n","$$\\phi^{n+1}_j=(1+c)\\phi^n_j-c\\phi^n_{j+1}$$\n","$$c=u\\frac{\\Delta t}{\\Delta x}$$\n","> Uses $\\phi^n_{j+1}$ to compute $\\phi_j^{n+1}$\n","  \n","  > Upstream for $u<0$. Stable.\n","  \n","  > Downstream for $u>0$. Unconditionally unstable.\n","  \n","  > Unconditionally unstable for solution with positive velocity.\n","\n","- FTBS: Forward in Time, Backwards in Space\n","$$\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_j-\\phi^n_j}{\\Delta t}+u\\frac{\\phi^n_j-\\phi^n_{j-1}}{\\Delta x}=0$$\n","$$\\phi^{n+1}_j=(1-c)\\phi^n_j+c\\phi^n_{j-1}$$\n","$$c=u\\frac{\\Delta t}{\\Delta x}$$\n","> Uses $\\phi^n_{j-1}$ to compute $\\phi_j^{n+1}$\n","  \n","  > Upstream for $u>0$. Conditionally stable (only when $0\\le c\\le1$)\n","  \n","  > Downstream for $u<0$. Unconditionally unstable.\n","\n","  > Conditionally stable for solution with positive velocity.\n","\n","- Upstream\n","\n","Computes new value by using old value in upstream point wrt advection velocity.\n","\n","- Downstream\n","\n","Computes new value by using old value in downstream point wrt advection velocity.\n","\n","- Von Neumann Stability Analysis\n","\n","Amplification factor must be bounded such that $|A|\\le1$ where $\\phi^n_j=A^ne^{ikj\\Delta x}$.\n","\n","Necessary for linear and nonlinear, but insufficient for nonlinear.\n","\n","- CFL: Courant-Friedrichs-Lewy condition\n","\n","> Time step $\\Delta t$ cannot exceed $\\frac{\\Delta x}{u}$.\n","\n","> Stable if $u\\Delta t\\le\\Delta x$\n","\n","> Unstable if $u\\Delta t>\\Delta x$\n","- Lax Theorem\n","\n","> No convergence if system is unstable.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"juxbmY0jJRso"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Exercise on upstream scheme\n","import numpy as np\n","from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n","\n","def phi0(x): #fxn for t=0, 40<=x<=70\n","    if (x>=40 and x<=70):\n","        return np.sin(np.pi*((x-40.)/30.))**2\n","    else:\n","        return 0.0\n","\n","def ftfs(phi_now): #forward time, forward space\n","    return (1+c)*phi_now-c*np.roll(phi_now,-1)\n","\n","def ftbs(phi_now): #forward time, backward space\n","    return (1-c)*phi_now+c*np.roll(phi_now,1)\n","\n","dx=0.10 #0.10m\n","u=0.087 #0.087m/s\n","dt=dx/u #dt=dx/u for c=1, no damping\n","c=u*dt/dx #c=1\n","t=0 #0s initial t\n","t1=1000 #1000s final t\n","x0=0 #0m initial x\n","x1=100 #100m final x\n","\n","x=np.arange(x0,x1,dx) #1D array of x-values between x0 and x1 with step nx\n","phi=[phi0(a) for a in x] #apply phi0 function to all x in array to fill phi array\n","phi=np.array(phi)\n","\n","while (t<t1):\n","    if (u>0):\n","        phi_new=ftbs(phi) #ftbs is stable if u>0\n","    else:\n","        phi_new=ftfs(phi) #ftfs is stable if u<0\n","    phi=phi_new\n","    if (t==0) or (round(t)%200==0):\n","        plt.plot(x,phi, label='ϕ('+str(round(t))+'s)')\n","    t=t+dt\n","\n","plt.xlabel('X')\n","plt.ylabel('ϕ(x)')\n","plt.legend(bbox_to_anchor=(1., 1.))\n","plt.grid()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":449},"id":"xXITHeJx_TtV","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1771942260852,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":599,"user":{"displayName":"BEATRICE BAYAN","userId":"07825214234165062643"}},"outputId":"9abc20a7-36ed-40c9-ba82-3b14805ffc59"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Lesson 3: Leapfrog Scheme\n","\n","- Linear Advection Equation\n","$$\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial t}+u\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial x}=0$$\n","- Analytical Solution\n","$$\\phi(x,t)=F(x-ut)$$\n","- Leapfrog Scheme: CTCS: Centered in Time, Centered in Space\n","$$\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_j-\\phi^{n-1}_j}{2\\Delta t}=-u\\frac{\\phi^n_{j+1}-\\phi^n_{j-1}}{2\\Delta x}$$\n","$$\\phi^{n+1}_j=\\phi^{n-1}_j-c(\\phi^n_{j+1}-\\phi^n_{j-1})$$\n","$$c=u\\frac{\\Delta t}{\\Delta x}$$\n","  \n","> Conditionally stable for solution with CFL condition:\n","$$|c|=|u|\\frac{\\Delta t}{\\Delta x}\\leq1$$\n","\n","- Robert-Asselin (RA) Filter\n","\n","To keep computational mode small.\n","\n","> Filter displacement:\n","$$d=\\alpha(\\phi^{n-1}-2\\phi^n+\\phi^{n+1})$$\n",">Applying in update:\n","$$\\hat{\\phi}^n=\\phi^n+d=(1-2\\alpha)\\phi^n+\\alpha(\\phi^{n+1}+\\phi^{n-1})$$\n","$$\\phi^{n-1}=\\hat{\\phi}^n$$\n","$$\\phi^n=\\phi^{n+1}$$\n","\n","- Robert-Asselin-William (RAW) Filter\n","\n","> Filter displacement:\n","$$d=\\alpha(\\phi^{n-1}-2\\phi^n+\\phi^{n+1})$$\n",">Applying in update:\n","$$\\hat{\\phi}^n=\\phi^n+\\beta d$$\n","$$\\hat{\\phi}^{n+1}=\\phi^{n+1}+(1-\\beta)d$$\n","$$\\phi^{n-1}=\\hat{\\phi}^n$$\n","$$\\phi^n=\\phi^{n+1}$$"],"metadata":{"id":"v0tvw8VDJYSZ"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Exercise on CTCS RAW scheme\n","import numpy as np\n","from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n","\n","def phi0(x): #phi(x,0)\n","    if (x<200):\n","        return 0.1\n","    elif (200<=x<250):\n","        return 2.0\n","    elif (250<=x<=300):\n","        return 1.0\n","    elif (x>300):\n","        return 0.1\n","\n","# NOTE --> You can initialize the profile in a single line in Python (see below)\n","#phi_old = np.where(x < 200, 0.1, np.where(x < 250, 2.0, np.where(x <= 300, 1.0, 0.1)))\n","\n","def ftfs(phi_now):\n","    return (1+c)*phi_now-c*np.roll(phi_now,-1)\n","\n","def ftbs(phi_now):\n","    return (1-c)*phi_now+c*np.roll(phi_now,1)\n","\n","def ctcs(phi_old,phi_now):\n","    return phi_old-c*(np.roll(phi_now,-1)-np.roll(phi_now,1))\n","\n","c=-0.1 #can also be -1.\n","dx=0.10 #0.10m\n","u=-0.31 #0.8m/s\n","\n","dt=c*dx/u #dt=dx/u for c=1, no damping\n","t=0 #0s initial t\n","t1=1000 #1000s final t\n","\n","x0=0 #0m initial x\n","x1=500 #500m final x\n","\n","alpha=0.05 #0.0 for no filter\n","beta=0.53 #0.0 for no filter\n","\n","x=np.arange(x0,x1,dx) #1D array of x-values between x0 and x1 with step nx\n","phi_old=[phi0(a) for a in x] #apply phi0 function to all x in array to fill phi array\n","phi_old=np.array(phi_old)\n","phi_now=phi_old.copy() #same dimensions\n","d=phi_old.copy() #same dimensions\n","\n","#stability condition\n","#using ftbs or ftfs for phi_now\n","if (u>0):\n","    phi_now=ftbs(phi_old)\n","else:\n","    phi_now=ftfs(phi_old)\n","\n","t=t+dt\n","\n","while(t<=t1+1):\n","    phi_new=ctcs(phi_old,phi_now) #using ctcs for everything else\n","    d=alpha*(phi_old+phi_new-2.0*phi_now) #RAW filter displacement\n","    phi_old=phi_now+beta*d #applying filtering in updating\n","    #for no beta:\n","    #phi_old=phi_now+d\n","    phi_now=phi_new+(1-beta)*d #applying filtering in updating\n","    #for no beta:\n","    #phi_now=phi_new\n","    if (t==0) or (round(t,2)%250.==0):\n","        plt.plot(x,phi_now, label='ϕ('+str(round(t))+'s)')\n","    t=t+dt\n","\n","plt.xlabel('X')\n","plt.ylabel('ϕ(x)')\n","plt.legend(bbox_to_anchor=(1., 1.))\n","plt.grid()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":449},"id":"qrts2DYLR3AO","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1772052890229,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":2494,"user":{"displayName":"BEATRICE BAYAN","userId":"07825214234165062643"}},"outputId":"03ab7a46-a305-4f7d-ed35-f652a65843c7"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Lesson 4: Semi-Lagrangian Scheme\n","\n","- Eulerian Linear Advection Equation\n","$$\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial t}+u\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial x}=0$$\n","- Analytical Solution\n","$$\\phi(x,t)=F(x-ut)$$\n","- Lagrangian Linear Advection Equation\n","$$\\frac{D\\phi}{Dt}=0$$\n","- Semi-Lagrangian Scheme\n","$$\\frac{\\phi(x_j,t^{n+1})-\\phi(depx_j,t^n)}{\\Delta t}=0$$\n","$$\\phi(x_j,t^{n+1})=\\phi(depx_j,t^n)$$\n","$$depx_j-x_j-u\\Delta t$$\n","$$u\\Delta t=(j-m+\\alpha)\\Delta x$$\n","$$depx_j=x_m-\\alpha\\Delta x$$\n","$$\\alpha=\\frac{x_m-depx_j}{\\Delta x}$$\n","- Linear Interpolation\n","$$\\phi^n(depx_j)=\\alpha\\phi^n(x_{m-1})+(1-\\alpha)\\phi^n(x_m)$$\n","- Cubic Interpolation\n","$$\\phi^n(depx_j)=-\\frac{\\alpha(1-\\alpha^2)}{6}\\phi^n(x_{m-2})+\\frac{\\alpha(1+\\alpha)(2-\\alpha)}{2}\\phi^n(x_{m-1})+\\frac{(1-\\alpha^2)(2-\\alpha)}{2}\\phi^n(x_m)-\\frac{\\alpha(1-\\alpha)(2-\\alpha)}{6}\\phi^n(x_{m+1})$$\n","- Stability\n","\n",">$|A|\\leq1$ if $0\\leq\\alpha\\leq1$.\n","\n","> Stable if interpolation points are two nearest to departure point. Neutral if $\\alpha=0$ or $\\alpha=1$, when no interpolation is needed.\n","\n","> Explicit since we use data points at n to compute next time index at n+1."],"metadata":{"id":"NZr7jqOdJgFK"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Exercise on Semi-Lagrangian Scheme\n","import numpy as np\n","from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n","\n","def phi0(x): #function phi(x,0)\n","    if (x<400):\n","        return 0.0\n","    elif (400<=x<500):\n","        return 0.1*(x-400.0)\n","    elif (500<=x<=600):\n","        return 20.0-0.1*(x-400.0)\n","    else:\n","        return 0.0\n","\n","xi=0.0\n","xf=1000.0\n","dx=0.5\n","\n","u=0.75\n","alpha=0.0\n","\n","t=0.0\n","tf=4000.0\n","dt=1\n","\n","x=np.arange(xi,xf+dx,dx) #fill until xf+dx\n","nx=len(x)\n","phi_now=[phi0(a) for a in x] #apply phi0 function to all x in array to fill phi array\n","phi_now=np.array(phi_now)\n","phi_new=phi_now.copy()\n","\n","while (t<=tf): #we want the last time step\n","    for j in range(nx): #start at 0\n","        xp=x[j] #take x as a point of reference\n","        xdep=xi+(xp-u*dt)%(xf-xi) #departure point\n","        if (xdep<xi):\n","            xdep=xf+xdep #periodic?\n","        m=int(np.floor(xdep/dx)) #m is m-1 in slides\n","        alpha=(xdep/dx)-m\n","        mp=m+1 #mp is m in slides\n","        mn=m-1 #mn is m-2 in slides\n","        mpp=m+2 #mp is m+1 in slides\n","        if (mp==nx):\n","            mp=0\n","        if (mpp==nx):\n","            mpp=0\n","        #linear interpolation\n","        #phi_new[j]=(1-alpha)*phi_now[mp]+alpha*phi_now[m]\n","        #cubic spline interpolation\n","        phi_new[j]=-(alpha*(1-alpha**2)/6)*phi_now[mn]+(alpha*(1+alpha)*(2-alpha)/2)*phi_now[m] + ((1-alpha**2)*(2-alpha)/2)*phi_now[mp] + (-alpha*(1-alpha)*(2-alpha)/6)*phi_now[mpp]\n","    phi_now[:]=phi_new[:]\n","    if (t%1000<dt):\n","        plt.plot(x, phi_new, label='ϕ('+str(round(t))+'s)')\n","    t=t+dt\n","\n","plt.xlabel('X')\n","plt.ylabel('ϕ(x)')\n","plt.legend()\n","bbox_to_anchor=(1., 1.)\n","plt.grid()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":449},"id":"7pueyMuLjhns","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1771942319950,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":53437,"user":{"displayName":"BEATRICE BAYAN","userId":"07825214234165062643"}},"outputId":"6e2c3055-c791-46f2-9005-248df7d2acbe"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Lesson 5: Diffusion Equation\n","\n","- Dirichlet Boundary Conditions\n","\n","Assume values of relevant quantity are imposed at boundaries of numerical grid (constant or f(t)).\n","\n","- von Neumann Boundary Conditions\n","\n","Assumes derivatives of relative quantities are imposed at boundaries of numerical grid (constant or f(t)).\n","\n","- Boundary Conditions describe the inherent geometry of the numerical domain.\n","\n","> Periodic - Assumes numerical domain is topologically connected in a given or in all directions.\n","\n","> Reflecting - Mimic the presence of reflecting boundary (zero transmission coefficient).\n","\n","> Absorbing - Mimic the presence of an absorbing boundary (unit transmission coefficient).\n","\n","- Heat or Diffusion Equation.\n","$$\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial t}=K\\frac{\\partial^2\\phi}{\\partial x^2}$$\n","\n","Linear Parabolic Equation. K is a constant.\n","\n","- Solution\n","Assuming:\n","$$\\frac{d\\phi}{dt}e^{ikx}=-k^2K\\phi(t)e^{ikx}$$\n","Integrating to find initial:\n","$$\\phi(t)=\\phi(0)e^{-k^2Kt}=e^{-k^2Kt}$$\n","Then the exact solution is:\n","$$\\phi(x,t)=e^{-k^2Kt}e^{ikx}$$\n","Standing wave, decreasing in amplitude, damping faster for short waves than long waves.\n","\n","- Centered Discretization\n","\n","Second-order accurate centered difference scheme:\n","$$\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_j-\\phi^{n-1}_j}{2\\Delta t}=K\\biggr(\\frac{\\phi^n_{j+1}-2\\phi^n_j+\\phi^n_{j-1}}{\\Delta x^2}\\biggr)$$\n","Substitute:\n","$$\\phi^n_j=A^ne^{ikj\\Delta x}$$\n","Unconditionally unstable for $A^-\\le-1$, and $0\\le A^+\\le1$ is physical mode.\n","\n","- Forward Discretization\n","\n","First-order forward difference for time derivative:\n","$$\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_j-\\phi^{n}_j}{\\Delta t}=K\\biggr(\\frac{\\phi^n_{j+1}-2\\phi^n_j+\\phi^n_{j-1}}{\\Delta x^2}\\biggr)$$\n","Dirichlet boundary condition:\n","$$x_N=x_0+N\\Delta x$$\n","$$\\phi(x_0)=\\phi_0 \\forall t$$\n","$$\\phi(x_N)=\\phi_N \\forall t$$\n","Conditionally stable $\\Delta t\\le\\frac{\\Delta x^2}{2K}$.\n","\n","Small increase in resolution requires big reduction in time step.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"7isVYBUVJlrD"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Exercise on Diffusion\n","import numpy as np\n","from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n","\n","xi=0\n","xf=1\n","dx=0.01\n","\n","K=2.9*10**(-5)\n","\n","t0=0\n","dt=1\n","t=t0\n","t1=60*60*6\n","\n","mult=K*dt/(dx**2) #forward difference coefficient\n","begin=0\n","end=-1\n","temp0=273.15\n","\n","def phi0(x): #phi(x,0) function\n","    if (0<=x<=0.5):\n","        return 273.15+20*x+np.sin(50*np.pi*x)\n","    elif (0.5<x<=1):\n","        return 273.15+20-20*x+np.sin(50*np.pi*x)\n","\n","def diffusion(phi_now,phi_new): #forward difference\n","    phi_new[begin]=temp0 #retaining constant heat at beginning\n","    phi_new[end]=temp0 #retaining constant heat at the end\n","    phi_new[begin+1:end]=phi_now[begin+1:end]+mult*(phi_now[begin+2:]-2.0*phi_now[begin+1:end]+phi_now[begin:end-1])\n","#python colon, stops before the :end value. If you want the last value, just do : without end.\n","#for the in-between, new is prev+coefficient*(etc...)\n","\n","x=np.arange(xi,xf+dx,dx)\n","phi_now=[phi0(a) for a in x]\n","phi_now=np.array(phi_now)\n","phi_new=phi_now.copy()\n","\n","while(t<t1):\n","    if (t%(60*60)==0):\n","        plt.plot(x, phi_new, label='ϕ('+str(round(t))+'s)')\n","    diffusion(phi_now,phi_new)\n","    phi_now=phi_new.copy()\n","    t=t+dt\n","\n","plt.xlabel('X')\n","plt.ylabel('ϕ(x)')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(visible=True)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":449},"id":"4G3ji2UGdw4K","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1771942439478,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":795,"user":{"displayName":"BEATRICE BAYAN","userId":"07825214234165062643"}},"outputId":"baef897f-9dd2-4372-9503-d0fed96c0671"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Lesson 6: Heat Transfer Equation\n","\n","- Heat or Diffusion Equation\n","\n","$$\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial t}=K\\frac{\\partial^2\\phi}{\\partial x^2}$$\n","\n","- Implicit formulation\n","\n","Evaluate instead at time $n+1$:\n","$$\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_j-\\phi^{n}_j}{\\Delta t}=K\\biggr(\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_{j+1}-2\\phi^{n+1}_j+\\phi^{n+1}_{j-1}}{\\Delta x^2}\\biggr)$$\n","\n","Using $\\alpha=\\frac{K\\Delta t}{\\Delta x^2}$:\n","$$\\phi^n_j=-\\alpha\\phi^{n+1}_{j+1}+(1+2\\alpha)\\phi^{n+1}_{j}-\\alpha\\phi^{n+1}_{j-1}$$\n","\n","Dirichlet boundary condition:\n","$$x_N=x_0+N\\Delta x$$\n","$$\\phi(x_0)=\\phi_0 \\forall t$$\n","$$\\phi(x_N)=\\phi_N \\forall t$$\n","Conditionally stable $\\Delta t\\le\\frac{\\Delta x^2}{2K}$.\n","\n","- TriDiagonal Matrix Form\n","\n","> Lower Diagonal: $A(2:N-1)$\n","\n","> Diagonal: $B(1:N-1)$\n","\n","> Upper Diagonal: $C(1:N-2)$\n","\n","- Thomas Algorithm\n","\n","> Forward Elimination. Aims to set all elements of lower diagonal to 0, and all elements of diagonal to 1.\n","\n","$$F_j=\\frac{c_j}{b_j-a_jF_{j-1}}$$\n","$$\\delta_j=\\frac{d_j-a_j\\delta_{j-1}}{b_j-a_jF_{j-1}}$$\n","\n","> Backward Substitution. Loops in reverse order over the elements to give us the solution.\n","\n","$$u_j=\\delta_j-F_ju_{j+1}$$\n","$$j\\in \\mathbb{N}[N-1,1]$$\n","\n","Implicit diffusion scheme is unconditionally stable."],"metadata":{"id":"M32PoxrgJrm7"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Exercise on Diffusion - TriDiagonal Matrix\n","import numpy as np\n","from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n","\n","xi=0\n","xf=1\n","dx=0.01\n","\n","K=2.9*10**(-5)\n","\n","t0=0\n","dt=1\n","t=t0\n","t1=60*60*6\n","\n","alpha=K*dt/(dx**2)\n","begin=0\n","end=-1\n","temp0=273.15\n","\n","def phi0(x): #phi(x,0)\n","    if (0<=x<=0.5):\n","        return 273.15+20*x+np.sin(50*np.pi*x)\n","    elif (0.5<x<=1):\n","        return 273.15+20-20*x+np.sin(50*np.pi*x)\n","\n","def diffusion(phi_now,phi_new): #forward difference\n","    phi_new[begin]=temp0 #Dirichlet boundary conditions\n","    phi_new[end]=temp0 #Dirichlet boundary conditions\n","    phi_new[begin+1:end]=phi_now[begin+1:end]+alpha*(phi_now[begin+2:]-2.0*phi_now[begin+1:end]+phi_now[begin:end-1])\n","\n","x=np.arange(xi,xf+dx,dx)\n","nx=len(x)\n","phi_now=[phi0(a) for a in x]\n","phi_now=np.array(phi_now)\n","phi_new=phi_now.copy()\n","\n","A=np.full((nx-2),-alpha) #lower diagonal\n","C=np.full((nx-2),-alpha) #upper diagonal\n","B=np.full((nx-1),1.0+2.0*-alpha) #diagonal\n","F=np.zeros(nx-1) #forward elimination F(x)\n","delta=np.zeros(nx-1) #forward elimination delta\n","\n","while(t<t1):\n","    if (t%(60*60)==0):\n","        plt.plot(x, phi_new, label='ϕ('+str(round(t))+'s)')\n","    diffusion(phi_now,phi_new)\n","    F[1]=0\n","    delta[0]=temp0\n","    for j in range(len(C)): #forward elimination\n","        F[j+1]=C[j]/(B[j+1]-A[j]*F[j])\n","        delta[j+1]=(phi_now[j+1]-A[j]*delta[j])/(B[j+1]-A[j]*F[j])\n","    phi_new[nx-1]=temp0\n","    for j in range(len(F),0): #backwards substitution\n","        phi_new[j]=delta[j]-F[j]*[phi_new[j+1]]\n","    phi_now=phi_new.copy()\n","    t=t+dt\n","\n","plt.xlabel('X')\n","plt.ylabel('ϕ(x)')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(visible=True)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":449},"id":"-zFCisOOd6Wg","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1771942467042,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":6794,"user":{"displayName":"BEATRICE BAYAN","userId":"07825214234165062643"}},"outputId":"3e01afb5-91cb-4f38-a640-957df4a4ae0c"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Lesson 7: Advection-Diffusion\n","\n","- Advection-Diffusion Problem\n","$$\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial t}+u\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial x}=K\\frac{\\partial^2\\phi}{\\partial x}$$\n","\n","> Leapfrog (CTCS) is conditionally stable for advection.\n","\n","> Forward approximation is conditionally stable for diffusion.\n","\n","- Discretization:\n","$$\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_j-\\phi^{n-1}_j}{2\\Delta t}+u\\frac{\\phi^n_{j+1}-\\phi^n_{j-1}}{2\\Delta x}=K\\biggr(\\frac{\\phi^{n-1}_{j+1}-2\\phi^{n-1}_j+\\phi^{n-1}_{j-1}}{\\Delta x^2}\\biggr)$$\n","\n","- Nonlinear Advection\n","\n","Flow itself is advected.\n","$$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t}+u\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}=0$$\n","\n","> Nonlinearity can cause numerical problems though truncation and stability.\n","\n","> Generates large gradients.\n","\n","> Simplest solution: use linear formulation and include diffusion to prevent formations of sharp gradients."],"metadata":{"id":"RmvcoS77Jyb2"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Exercise on Advection-Diffusion\n","import numpy as np\n","from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n","\n","def phi0(x): #phi(x,0)\n","    if (x<400):\n","        return 0.0\n","    elif (400<=x<500):\n","        return 0.01*(x-400.0)\n","    elif (500<=x<=600):\n","        return 2.0-0.01*(x-400.0)\n","    else:\n","        return 0.0\n","\n","def ftcs_diff(p_now): #forward in time, centered in space + diffusion\n","    return p_now-0.5*c*(np.roll(p_now,-1)-np.roll(p_now,1))+dc*(np.roll(p_now,-1)-2.0*p_now+np.roll(p_now,1))\n","\n","def ctcs_diff(p_old,p_now): #leapfrog, centered in time, centered in space  diffusion\n","    return p_old-c*(np.roll(p_now,-1)-np.roll(p_now,1))+2.0*dc*(np.roll(p_old,-1)-2.0*p_old+np.roll(p_old,1))\n","\n","K=0.029\n","\n","xi=0.0\n","xf=1000.0\n","dx=0.2\n","\n","u=0.95\n","alpha=0.1 #0 without RAW filter\n","beta=0.53 #1 without RAW filter\n","\n","t0=0.0\n","t1=2000.0\n","\n","c=0.3\n","dt=c*dx/u\n","dc=K*dt/(dx**2) #alpha\n","\n","x=np.arange(xi,xf+dx,dx)\n","p_now=[phi0(a) for a in x]\n","p_now=np.array(p_now)\n","p_old=p_now.copy()\n","p_new=p_now.copy()\n","\n","p_now=ftcs_diff(p_old) #only for initial time field\n","plt.plot(x, p_now, label='phi('+str(round(t0))+'s)')\n","\n","t=t0+dt\n","\n","while(t<=t1):\n","    if (round(t,1)%500.==0 and round(t,1)!=round(t-dt,1)):\n","        plt.plot(x, p_now, label='ϕ('+str(round(t))+'s)')\n","    p_new=ctcs_diff(p_old,p_now) #ctcs for rest of field\n","    d=alpha*(p_old+p_new-2.0*p_now) #RAW Filter displacement\n","    p_old=p_now+beta*d #RAW filter update\n","    p_now=p_new+(1-beta)*d #RAW filter update\n","    t=t+dt\n","\n","plt.xlabel('X')\n","plt.ylabel('ϕ(x)')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(visible=True)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":449},"id":"2qqwe27id9Zj","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1771942491493,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":5780,"user":{"displayName":"BEATRICE BAYAN","userId":"07825214234165062643"}},"outputId":"7a0e1a10-4016-4660-ae14-76532eaa3a32"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Lesson 8: 1D Gravity Wave\n","\n","- 1D Shallow Water Equations, Neglect Coriolis, Linearized about a state of rest $u-0$, $\\Phi=gH$.\n","\n","Momentum:\n","$$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial x}=0$$\n","\n","Mass:\n","$$\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial t}+\\Phi\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}=0$$\n","\n","Solutions:\n","$$u(x,t)=\\hat{u}e^{i(kx-\\omega t})$$\n","$$\\phi(x,t)=\\hat{\\phi}e^{i(kx-\\omega t)}$$\n","\n","Dispersion Relation:\n","$$\\omega^2=k^2\\Phi$$\n","\n","Solutions are non-dispersive waves with all the same phase speed:\n","$$\\frac{\\omega}{k}=\\sqrt{\\Phi}$$\n","\n","Periodic domain initial conditions:\n","$$\\phi(x,0)=F(x)$$\n","$$u(x,0)=0$$\n","\n","Solution:\n","$$\\phi(x,t)=\\frac{1}{2}F(x-at)+\\frac{1}{2}F(x+at)$$\n","\n","- Discretization Method 1\n","\n","Second-order centered differences in space and time:\n","$$\\frac{u^{n+1}_j-u^{n-1}_j}{2\\Delta t}+\\frac{\\phi^n_{j+1}-\\phi^n_{j-1}}{2\\Delta x}=0$$\n","$$\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_j-\\phi^{n-1}_j}{2\\Delta t}+\\Phi\\frac{u^n_{j+1}-u^n_{j-1}}{2\\Delta x}=0$$\n","\n","Rearranging for the unknowns:\n","$$u^{n+1}_j=u^{n-1}_j-\\frac{\\Delta t}{\\Delta x}(\\phi^n_{j+1}-\\phi^n_{j-1})$$\n","$$\\phi^{n+1}_j=\\phi^{n-1}_j-\\Phi\\frac{\\Delta t}{\\Delta x}(u^n_{j+1}-u^n_{j-1})$$\n","\n",">If $|c|\\le1$ then the square root is purely imaginary and $|A^2| = 1$; the scheme is stable.\n","\n",">If $|c|>1$ then for some value of $k$ the square root is real, $|A^2|>1$ for at least one of the roots, and the scheme is unstable.\n","\n","- Discretization Method 2\n","\n","Center in space and forward/backward time:\n","$$\\frac{u^{n+1}_j-u^{n}_j}{\\Delta t}+\\frac{\\phi^n_{j+1}-\\phi^n_{j-1}}{2\\Delta x}=0$$\n","$$\\frac{\\phi^{n+1}_j-\\phi^{n-1}}{\\Delta t}+\\Phi\\frac{u^{n+1}_{j+1}-u^{n+1}_{j-1}}{2\\Delta x}=0$$\n","\n","Rearranging for the unknowns:\n","$$u^{n+1}_j=u^n_j-\\frac{\\Delta t}{2\\Delta x}(\\phi^n_{j+1}-\\phi^n_{j-1})$$\n","$$\\phi^{n+1}_j=\\phi^n_j-\\Phi\\frac{\\Delta t}{2\\Delta x}(u^{n+1}_{j+1}-u^{n+1}_{j-1})$$\n","\n",">For $|c| < 2$ we obtain $|A|^2 = 1$, and thus the scheme is stable and we do not have damping.\n","\n",">For $|c| > 2$, for some $k$ the amplification factor can be greater than one, and thus the scheme is unstable.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"S9BTXAvvJ4Nw"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Exercise on Gravity Waves - Method 1\n","import numpy as np\n","from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n","\n","def phi0(x): #phi(x,0)\n","    if (x<400):\n","        return 0.0\n","    elif (400<=x<600):\n","        return np.sin(((x-400)/200)*np.pi)**2\n","    else:\n","        return 0.0\n","\n","xi=0.0\n","xf=1000.0\n","dx=0.5\n","\n","t0=0.0\n","t1=2000.0\n","dt=0.1\n","\n","dtdx=dt/dx\n","P=1.0\n","c=np.sqrt(P)*dtdx\n","\n","def ueq_ft(u_now,p_now):\n","    return u_now-0.5*dtdx*(np.roll(p_now,-1)-np.roll(p_now,1))\n","\n","def peq_ft(p_now,u_fut):\n","    return p_now-c*0.5*(np.roll(u_now,-1)-np.roll(u_now,1))\n","\n","def ueq(u_old,p_now):\n","    return u_old-dtdx*(np.roll(p_now,-1)-np.roll(p_now,1))\n","\n","def peq(p_old,u_now):\n","    return p_old-c*(np.roll(u_now,-1)-np.roll(u_now,1))\n","\n","x=np.arange(xi,xf+dx,dx)\n","p_now=[phi0(a) for a in x] #apply phi0 function to all x in 